e to lower casino and rooms revenue, partially offset by lower operating expenses.","context":"Adjusted Property EBITDAR at Wynn Palace decreased $50.8 million for the year ended December 31, 2025 primarily due to a $53.4 million decrease in rooms revenue.","section":"Segment Information","block":541,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001174922-26-000013","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-03-02","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001174922","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1174922/000117492226000013/wynn-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/ea305ccae85b5bb9041ba8213a20592c9b68fbeff4f04b8b38648c3fca68e452.bin","sha256":"ea305ccae85b5bb9041ba8213a20592c9b68fbeff4f04b8b38648c3fca68e452"}},{"id":"ac1bdb400bef44cd1c00c230c702acf03c645bd7c0a317ef27e98d334c662a1a","quote":"Adjusted Property EBITDAR at our Las Vegas Operations for the year ended December 31, 2025, decreased $44.4 million, primarily due to a decrease of $48.1 million in non-gaming revenues, partially offset by lower operating expenses. The year ended December 31, 2024, included incremental food and beverage revenue from Super Bowl-related events and from outlets undergoing renovations.","context":"Adjusted Property EBITDAR at Wynn Macau decreased $39.7 million for the year ended December 31, 2025, due to a decrease in operating revenues of $54.0 million, largely attributable to lower casino and rooms revenue, partially offset by lower operating expenses.","section":"Segment Information","block":542,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001174922-26-000013","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-03-02","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001174922","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1174922/000117492226000013/wynn-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/ea305ccae85b5bb9041ba8213a20592c9b68fbeff4f04b8b38648c3fca68e452.bin",